(7424898, 1130313, 86447, '<td valign="top">Greetings From the Critique Club, Don!<br/> <br/>I apologize for the late critique... the queue has been backed up for a long while.   We seem to have the new requests under control and have started on the backlog from long ago.<br/> <br/>Anyway, to the matter at hand.<br/> <br/>What a wonderful image of a rather boring subject!<br/> <br/>You''ve really gotten a lot of mileage out of an ear of corn.  I love those silks... creating havoc and excitement.  Your use of strong lighting also adds to the interest of the image.  Well done!<br/> <br/> <br/>For the record, I disagree with the comment asking for fill light on the dark side.  I think that the mystery is my favorite part of the image.  <br/> <br/>I might have cropped the bottom off... so that the bright spots don''t overpower the mystery... but that''s my only nitpick.<br/> <br/>Congratulations again on your HM!</td>', 'Greetings From the Critique Club, Don! I apologize for the late critique... the queue has been backed up for a long while.   We seem to have the new requests under control and have started on the backlog from long ago. Anyway, to the matter at hand. What a wonderful image of a rather boring subject! You''ve really gotten a lot of mileage out of an ear of corn.  I love those silks... creating havoc and excitement.  Your use of strong lighting also adds to the interest of the image.  Well done!  For the record, I disagree with the comment asking for fill light on the dark side.  I think that the mystery is my favorite part of the image.   I might have cropped the bottom off... so that the bright spots don''t overpower the mystery... but that''s my only nitpick. Congratulations again on your HM!', '2015-12-30 17:33:51.000000', NULL, 0);
